  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Sorting Office",
    "overview": "Every packet is addressed mail. Sources arrive on the left, are read at a sorting frame that has one pigeonhole column per real pipeline stage (Parse, Lists, Bans, IDS, State, Rules, Policy), and either continue to their service on the right or drop into the bin of the stage that held them. The console is built for an examiner on a projector, a student learning, and an operator in a long session, so it is dense but calm: charcoal steps for structure, colour reserved for state, and every figure traceable to the packets behind it.\n\nThe ground is near-black charcoal and panels are slightly lighter charcoal with no border and no shadow. Words are set in Public Sans and ranked by weight and ink, not by size; addresses, ports, timestamps and counts are set in JetBrains Mono like labels on an envelope. Selection is never a fill or a glow: it is a single 1px ink line. Verdicts always carry a shape as well as a colour, so the console reads the same in greyscale.\n\nThe category default, a KPI-card grid over a line chart and an alerts table, is the explicit anti-reference. The figures are one divided strip, and the hero is a flow map of real traffic.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Charcoal tonal layering; no borders on panels, no shadows at rest.",
      "Colour means state only: teal forwarded, coral held, amber IDS and rate limits.",
      "Shape plus colour for every verdict: ring, 45-degree hatch, diamond, hollow circle.",
      "Mono for every network value; sans for every word.",
      "Selection is a 1px ink line.",
      "Motion is state feedback and real packet dots, nothing else."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Colour Is State Rule",
        "body": "Teal, coral and amber appear only where they mean forwarded, held, or inspected. Nothing decorative is tinted.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Neutral Witness Rule",
        "body": "Status that is not a verdict stays grey: the disconnected stamp is a grey dot and paper ink, and the simulated and capture-replay source badges are grey. Only a live packet source shows teal, because live capture is the forwarding path working.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Envelope Rule",
        "body": "Addresses, ports, protocols, timestamps, byte offsets and counts are always mono; labels and sentences are never mono. This is a user requirement, not decoration.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rank By Ink Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from weight (400, 500, 600) and ink (text, muted, faint), not from new sizes. Uppercase labels and tracked-out caps are not part of the system.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Desk Rule",
        "body": "Anything that stays on screen sits flat; only a tooltip that follows the pointer may cast a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** mark selection with the 1px paper-ink line and nothing else.",
      "**Do** pair every verdict colour with its shape and word: ring, hatch, diamond, hollow circle.",
      "**Do** set every address, port, timestamp and count in JetBrains Mono, and every word in Public Sans.",
      "**Do** open each view with title, finding line, source badge and freshness stamp.",
      "**Do** use one width scale across a flow map and draw only real sampled packets.",
      "**Do** put loading, empty and error states inside the block they belong to.",
      "**Do** keep state transitions between 150 and 250ms and honour prefers-reduced-motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use teal, coral or amber for anything that is not forwarded, held, or inspected; keep the source badge (except live) and the disconnected stamp grey.",
      "**Don't** add borders or shadows to panels; only floating tips use the float shadow.",
      "**Don't** build a KPI-card grid; figures live in one divided strip with the lead largest.",
      "**Don't** introduce uppercase eyebrows, kickers or tracked caps above headings.",
      "**Don't** animate anything except state feedback and packet dots."
    ]
  }
}